<title>DENMARK: Danish Economy Ministry report - main figures.</title>
<headline>Danish Economy Ministry report - main figures.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a table of the main points from the latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast (percent growth) issued on Tuesday. Estimates from last forecast in December 1996 in brackets.</p>
<p>					1997	     1998</p>
<p>GDP				   3.3 (2.9)	3.0 (2.7)</p>
<p>Inflation			   2.3 (2.3)	2.4 (2.3)</p>
<p>Private consumption	     2.7 (2.5)	3.1 (3.0)</p>
<p>Exports			     4.3 (4.1)	4.5 (4.6)</p>
<p>Imports			     4.1 (3.6)	4.2 (4.6)</p>
<p>Unemployment			7.8 (8.0)	7.4 (7.6)</p>
<p>C/a surplus (billion crowns)  12.0 (13.0)   13.0 (15.0)</p>
<p>Govt public sector expenditure (bln crowns)</p>
<p>					+7.0 (+2.0)   +8.0 (+4.8)</p>
<p>10-yr interest rate  (pct/yr)</p>
<p>					 6.7 (6.7)     6.6 (6.6)</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
